 ### 2.6 Where the trunk IMU is wired
 
+**Moving-head HAT BMI088 (`head_bmi088`).** This explicit Feetech source subscribes to
+`head_imu.stream` on `head_socket` (default `/run/tofd/tof.sock`); tofd remains the only I2C
+owner. It never identifies or reads ID 200. The reader checks the BMI088 subscription,
+source sequence, finite values and `CLOCK_MONOTONIC` sample age before publishing a raw
+sensor snapshot. A disconnected or restarted stream clears the snapshot and starts a new
+epoch; the existing one-second settling gate still applies.
+
+Commissioning and FeetechIo each keep eight complete measured ID 30–33 encoder packets.
+Two packets must bracket the IMU's source timestamp, 5–40 ms apart and no more than 50 ms
+old. No encoder extrapolation, stale cache or commanded joint target is substituted.
+`head_estimator_library` loads the local ABI-v1 `microduck_estimate_encoders` C++ core once,
+outside the tick. That core interpolates angles and removes head angular velocity:
+`q_WB = q_WS inverse(q_BS)` and `omega_B = R_BS omega_S - J(q) qdot`.
+
+`[imu_mounts.head_bmi088] quat` means **sensor-to-model-head-site**, unlike the fixed-body
+sources. The compensated reading is already body-frame, so TrunkFrame uses identity and
+retains its readiness/median gates. The fixed-body `verify-imu` command explicitly refuses
+this source: its upright check cannot certify a moving head mount. Until mounting axes and
+head joint directions are physically validated with the torso fixed, its source-specific
+`verified` flag stays false and motion remains disabled. Diagnostic estimates alone never
+authorize motion. Head translational acceleration can still bias tofd's Madgwick attitude;
+the implementation does not claim to remove that effect. Raw `--read-only` telemetry is
+explicitly marked sensor-frame and uncompensated.
+
 By default, and originally, the trunk IMU is the `imu_to_dxl` board: ID 200 on the servo bus,
 read in the servos' own `sync_read` (§1.1). On the Feetech backend (`bus.protocol = "feetech"`)
 `[trunk_imu] source` can name a module on the board's own I²C instead — `bno08x` (BNO085/BNO086,
